1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
That high-pitched squeal
when you start your car?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
That is not your brakes.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,600
It is usually the serpentine belt —

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
one belt running your AC,
power steering, and alternator.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Cold mornings make it worse.

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
The rubber stiffens, slips on the
pulley, and squeals until it warms up.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
But a belt that slips today
can crack and snap later —

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
and take your alternator's
charging with it.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Hear it every cold start?
Get the belt checked before it strands you.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Nick's Tire and Auto — link in bio.
